-# Transcript Saver v3 — Floating Sphere + Folders + Auto-Save
+# Transcripts Page (final design)
 
-This updates the Transcript Saver to a **floating sphere + full-screen overlay** design
-with **named folders** and **fully automatic saving**. It builds on top of the v2
-Transcript Saver and the v1 playlist batch feature.
+The saver is now a **proper page in the sidebar** — the natural fit for this app
+(every feature here is a page: Download, History, Whisper, Library, Playlist…).
+The floating-sphere/overlay experiment is removed.
 
 ---
 
-## What changed (v3)
-
-### 1. Floating sphere → full-screen overlay
-- A small **floating sphere** (bottom-right, with a count badge) sits near the
-  **URL Transcript** section on the Download page.
-- Clicking the sphere opens the Transcript Saver as a **full-screen overlay**
-  (covers the whole screen). Click **Close** (or the X) to return.
-- The URL Transcript panel also has an **Open Saver** button.
-
-### 2. Transcript cards (like YouTube thumbnails)
-- Saved transcripts appear as a grid of **square cards**.
-- Each card shows the **title + the first few lines of the transcript** (the
-  "thumbnail"), plus the folder, source and line count.
-- Clicking a card expands it to show the **full transcript**; there are also
-  **Copy**, **Edit** and **Delete** buttons right on the card.
-
-### 3. Named folders + first-come-first-serve (General)
-- When you pick a download range in **"Download a Range from a Playlist"** and tick
-  **"Also fetch YouTube auto transcript"**, a **"Save transcripts into folder"** box
-  appears — type any folder name (e.g. `Calculus Lectures`).
-- Every auto-fetched transcript is saved **in parallel** with the download into that
-  folder. If you leave the box empty, transcripts land in **General**
-  (first-come-first-serve).
-- The overlay has **folder chips** (All / General / each named folder) to filter the
-  cards.
-
-### 4. No manual saving — it's automatic
-- Fetching a transcript in the **URL Transcript** panel (paste link + Enter) now
-  **auto-saves** it into the saver (General folder) — nothing to click.
-- Fetches inside the overlay ("Fetch & save") also auto-save into the folder you
-  typed there.
-- Batch downloads auto-save every fetched transcript into the chosen folder.
-- Everything persists in the database — survives video deletion, cache clears and
-  page reloads. **Clear all** (click twice to confirm) empties everything, or delete
-  individual cards.
-
----
-
-## New/updated backend fields
-
-- `saved_transcripts.folder` column (auto-migrated on existing installs; empty =
-  General).
-- `POST /api/playlist/download` accepts `transcript_folder` (folder name for the
-  auto-fetched transcripts).
-- `POST /api/transcript-saver` accepts `folder`.
-- `POST /api/transcript-saver/fetch` accepts `folder` (request body `{url, folder}`).
-- `PATCH /api/transcript-saver/{id}` accepts `folder`.
+## How it works
+
+### The "Transcripts" page (sidebar → Transcripts)
+- **Sidebar item "Transcripts"** with a live count badge (number of saved transcripts).
+- Top panel: **Fetch & save** — paste a YouTube link (+ optional folder) and its auto
+  transcript is fetched and saved instantly. No manual save step.
+- **Search box** filters by title / text / URL / folder.
+- **Folder chips** (All / General / each named folder) filter the list.
+- Each saved transcript is a **card** showing the **first few lines** (like a preview).
+  Click a card to **read the full transcript**; each card has **Copy**, **Edit** and
+  **Delete** buttons.
+- **Clear all** (click twice to confirm) empties everything; **Refresh** reloads.
+
+### Automatic saving (you never save manually)
+1. **URL Transcript panel (Download page):** paste a link and press **Get Transcript** →
+   it fetches, shows the transcript, and **auto-saves it** to Transcripts (General
+   folder) with a toast. A **View Transcripts** link next to the panel takes you to the page.
+2. **Playlist batch downloads:** tick *"Also fetch YouTube auto transcript"* + enter a
+   **folder name** → every video's transcript is fetched **in parallel** with the
+   download and saved into that folder. Empty folder = **General** (first-come-first-serve).
+
+### Persistence
+Transcripts are stored in the SQLite `saved_transcripts` table. They survive video
+deletion, cache clears and page reloads. The sidebar badge updates automatically.
 
